          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            The <strong class="text-white">best canoe for river paddling</strong> is the one whose rocker, length, and hull material match the water you actually paddle. For most people that is the <strong class="text-white">Mad River Explorer 16</strong> — agile enough for rapids, efficient enough for the flat miles between them, and forgiving when leaned. If your river is rocky and technical, the <strong class="text-white">Esquif Prospecteur 15</strong> in T-Formex is the durability and handling upgrade worth paying for. If your days are long and your water is wide, the <strong class="text-white">Old Town Penobscot 164</strong> will get you further with less effort.
